Fix the crash when a monitor is unplugged (or drops out on suspend/wake).

Upstream issue: https://github.com/quickshell-mirror/quickshell/issues/910 (open as of 2026-10-18).

When a screen goes away the compositor closes its layer surfaces, Quickshell detaches each
window's content item and deletes the window. An item that is the source of a
ShaderEffectSource (Caelestia's desktop clock blurs `behindClock`, the wallpaper) keeps one
extra reference to that window, so it keeps a dangling window pointer; when the per-screen
delegate is destroyed a moment later, Qt derefs the freed window and segfaults in
QQuickWindowPrivate::cleanup(). The fix drops any references to the old window still left in
the content tree right after detaching it.

Reproduced and verified in a nested Hyprland with `hyprctl output create/remove headless`:
stock build crashes on the first unplug, patched build survived 60+ unplugs incl. rapid flaps.

diff --git a/src/window/proxywindow.cpp b/src/window/proxywindow.cpp
index bc0181c..c99ec0c 100644
--- a/src/window/proxywindow.cpp
+++ b/src/window/proxywindow.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #include "proxywindow.hpp"
 #include <functional>
 
+#include <private/qquickitem_p.h>
 #include <private/qquickwindow_p.h>
 #include <qcontainerfwd.h>
 #include <qcoreevent.h>
@@ -33,6 +34,23 @@
 #include "../debug/lint.hpp"
 #include "windowinterface.hpp"
 
+namespace {
+
+// Detaching the content item from a window derefs every item under it, but an item can hold more
+// than one reference to its window (shader effect sources and layers take extra ones on their
+// source item). If those aren't all given back before the window is deleted, the item keeps a
+// dangling window pointer and crashes Qt when it is later reparented or destroyed, which is what
+// happens when a screen is removed (layer surface closed, then its windows destroyed).
+// Drop whatever references to the old window are still left in the tree.
+void releaseStaleWindowRefs(QQuickItem* item, QQuickWindow* window) {
+	auto* d = QQuickItemPrivate::get(item);
+	while (d->window == window) d->derefWindow();
+
+	for (auto* child: d->childItems) releaseStaleWindowRefs(child, window);
+}
+
+} // namespace
+
 ProxyWindowBase::ProxyWindowBase(QObject* parent)
     : Reloadable(parent)
     , mContentItem(new ProxyWindowContentItem()) {
@@ -185,6 +203,7 @@ ProxiedWindow* ProxyWindowBase::disownWindow(bool keepItemOwnership) {
 
 	if (!keepItemOwnership) {
 		this->mContentItem->setParentItem(nullptr);
+		releaseStaleWindowRefs(this->mContentItem, this->window);
 	}
 
 	auto* window = this->window;
